    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d419">

                <pb facs="0367" n="355" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg355"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.7962/32½: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Walton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-01-21T13:00:00-00:44">January 21, 1942—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 23—12:27 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>14. If report is true that Pan American engineers have been instructed to have
                    Roberts Field in readiness for landing of bombers by January 26, Legation
                    suggests that Liberian Government be approached for necessary permission.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Walton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
